{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And you came near and stood under the mountain, etc. — as it is written: ויוצא משה את העם לקראת האלהים מן המחנה ויתיצבו בתחתית ההר. Anything high relative to something low: the high one is called 'upon' and the low one 'under' — ישב פתח האהל / נצבים עליו. And likewise תחת ההר — because they are low and the mountain is higher than they are. And it was necessary to write it here, as it is written before us: ועתה למה נמות כי תאכלנו האש הגדולה וגו׳."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Rashbam cites Exodus 19:17 and apparently also Exodus 33:8 (ישב פתח האהל / נצבים עליו) to illustrate that 'under' and 'upon' are relative terms between high and low."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:49.625563782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}